---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Glossary
eyebrow: Reference
subtitle: Every piece of jargon we use in the docs, explained in plain language.
permalink: /glossary/
---
<div class="lead" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
  Software has vocabulary. Publishing software has more. This page is a standing translator, hover the underlined terms anywhere on the site to get a short definition, or read the full entries below.
</div>

<nav class="glossary-alpha" aria-label="Jump to letter">
  {% set letters = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ" | split("") %}
  {% for letter in letters %}
    {% set hasTerm = false %}
    {% for entry in glossary %}
      {% if (entry.term[0] | upper) == letter %}{% set hasTerm = true %}{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if hasTerm %}
      <a href="#letter-{{ letter | lower }}">{{ letter }}</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="glossary-alpha__inactive" aria-disabled="true">{{ letter }}</span>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</nav>

<div class="glossary-list">
  {% set lastLetter = "" %}
  {% for entry in glossary %}
    {% set letter = entry.term[0] | upper %}
    {% if letter != lastLetter %}
      <h2 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-{{ letter | lower }}">{{ letter }}</h2>
      {% set lastLetter = letter %}
    {% endif %}
    <article class="glossary-entry" id="term-{{ entry.term | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}">
      <h3 class="glossary-entry__term">
        {{ entry.term }}
        {% if entry.alt %}<span class="glossary-entry__alt">· also {{ entry.alt }}</span>{% endif %}
      </h3>
      <p class="glossary-entry__short">{{ entry.short }}</p>
      {% if entry.long %}<p class="glossary-entry__long">{{ entry.long }}</p>{% endif %}
    </article>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">
  <div class="callout__title">Term missing?</div>
  <p>If the docs use a word we haven't defined, <a href="/forms/docs-feedback/">let me know</a>. I'll add it to the glossary.</p>
</div>
